# ROM / firmware images and other binary assets must never be EOL-converted.
#
# Git guesses "text vs binary" by looking for NUL bytes, and some ROM images
# have none — bkdsp01.bin is 117 bytes of I8039 code followed by 0xFF padding,
# so Git classified it as text. With core.autocrlf=true a checkout would then
# rewrite its single 0x0A byte as 0x0D 0x0A and hand you a corrupted dump.
# Mark every image type explicitly instead of relying on the heuristic.

*.bin   binary
*.bin2  binary
*.rom   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.png   binary
*.sal   binary
